                      %a{:href => "/nlab/edit/type+theory+-+contents"} Edit this sidebar
          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#formalizations"} Formalizations
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#RussellStyle"} Russell universe
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#TarskiStyle"} Tarski universes
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#other_universes"} Other universes
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#UniverseEnlargement"} Universe enlargement
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#extensionality_principle_of_type_universes"} Extensionality principle of type universes
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#cumulativity"} Cumulativity
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#CategoricalSemantics"} Categorical semantics
              %li
                %a{:href => "#other_types_of_types"} Other types of types
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#as_a_strict_tarski_universe"} As a strict Tarski universe
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#as_a_weak_tarski_universe"} As a weak Tarski universe
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#as_a_russell_universe"} As a Russell universe
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            %em type universe
            – usually written
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒰
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Type
            – is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terms"} terms
            are either themselves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} types
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Russell+universes"}> Russell universes
            ), or representations of types in an internal model of the type theory (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tarski+universes"}> Tarski universes
            ). Either way, it is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universe"} universe
            of (small)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} types
            = succeed "," do
              %em universe in type theory
            = succeed "." do
              %em type of types
          %p#TypeUniverseAsReflection
            One also speaks of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒰
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
            as being a
            %em reflection
            of the type system in itself (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#MartinLoef74"} MartinLöf 74, p. 6
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Palmgren"} Palmgren, pp. 2-3
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Rathjen"} Rathjen, p. 1
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Luo11"} Luo 11, section 2.5
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Luo12"} Luo 12, p. 2
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#SEP"} Stanf. Enc. Phil.
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflection+principle"} reflection principle
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            a type of (small) types is what in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            is interpreted as a (small)
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object+classifier"} object classifier
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+propositions"} type of propositions
            which only contains the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28-1%29-truncated"} (-1)-truncated
            = succeed "-1" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-level"} h-level
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifier"} subobject classifier
          %p
            In the presence of a type universe a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgement"} judgement
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝒰
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\vdash A : \mathcal{U}
          %p
            says that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/term"} term
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒰
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            itself (for Russell universes), or a representation of types in an internal model of the type theory (for Tarski universes).
          %p
            More generally, in Russell universes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypothetical+judgement"} hypothetical judgement
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝒰
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  x : X \vdash A(x) : \mathcal{U}
          %p
            says that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type"} dependent type
          %p In Tarski universes the corresponding hypothetical judgment would be of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi El
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  x : X \vdash El(A)(x)\; type
          %p
            Type universes are important in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            for numerous reasons:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                Dependent type theory with a separate
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgment"} judgment
                serves as a background for a variety of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations+of+mathematics"} foundations of mathematics
                via the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions+as+some+types"} propositions as some types
                interpretation of dependent type theory: One can add a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/von+Neumann+universe"} von Neumann universe
                to the dependent type theory and work entirely in the von Neumann universe for
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/material+set+theory"} material set theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sets"} category of sets
                to the dependent type theory and work entirely in the category of sets for
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structural+set+theory"} structural set theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+all+propositions"} type of all propositions
                and a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+type"} natural numbers type
                and work in the dependent type theory itself for
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher-order+logic"} higher-order logic
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+type+theory"} univalent type theory
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+foundations"} univalent foundations
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axioms"} axioms
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+schemata"} axiom schemata
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universe+extensionality"} universe extensionality
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+resizing"} propositional resizing
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+replacement"} replacement
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+infinity"} infinity
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} choice
            %li
              %p
                In
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+quantifier"} universal quantifier
                and the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/existential+quantifier"} existential quantifier
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgment"} judged
                separately as a type, and thus it is impossible to quantify over types. Quantification over types is necessary for proving
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+properties"} universal properties
                of various
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+structures"} mathematical structures
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
                are the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            %li
              %p
                Having a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hierarchy+of+universes"} hierarchy of universes
                where every type is an element of the hierarchy, instead of a single separate type judgment has its own benefits. These includes the lack of annotations in defining types, since all types are elements of universes
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A:U_i
                and all family of types are elements of function types
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B:A \to U_i
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objective+type+theory"} objective type theory
                which does not have
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgmental+equality"} judgmental equality
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+context"} split context
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+type+theory"} modal type theory
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            the type universe
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒰
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
            is often assumed to satisfy the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence"} univalence
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom"} axiom
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object+classifier"} object classifier
            is part of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} internal (∞,1)-category
            in the ambient
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+category"} indexed category
            is the small
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain+fibration"} codomain fibration
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Per+Martin-Lof"}> Per Martin-Lof
            ‘s original type theory contained a Russell universe which contained
            %em all
            types, which therefore in particular contained itself, i.e. one had
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Type
                    %mo :
                    %mi Type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Type : Type
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Yves+Girard"} Jean-Yves Girard
            that this was inconsistent; see
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Girard%27s+paradox"} Girard's paradox
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hierarchy+of+universes"} hierarchy of universes
          %h2#formalizations Formalizations
          %h3#RussellStyle Russell universe
          %p
            A
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Russell+universe"} Russell universe
            or
            %strong universe à la Russell
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            whose terms
            %em are
            types. In the presence of a separate
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgment"} judgment
            “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \;type
            ”, this can be formulated as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+deduction"} deduction rule
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi 𝒰
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{A:\mathcal{U}}{A \;type}
          %p
            Thus, the
            %a{:href => "natural+deduction#IntroductionAndElimination"} type formers
            have rules saying which universe they belong to, such as:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi 𝒰
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi B
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi 𝒰
                    %mrow
                      %mi Π
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi B
                      %mo :
                      %mi 𝒰
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{A:\mathcal{U}\quad B:A\to \mathcal{U}}{\Pi\, A\, B : \mathcal{U}}
          %p
            With Russell universes, we can also omit the judgment “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\; type
            ” and replace it everywhere by a judgment that A is a term of some universe. This is the approach taken in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#UFP13"} UFP13
          %h3#TarskiStyle Tarski universes
          %p
            A
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tarski+universe"} Tarski universe
            or a
            %strong universe à la Tarski
            (
            %a{:href => "#Hofmann"}> Hofmann, section 2.1.6
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Luo12"} Luo 12
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Gallozzi14"} Gallozzi 14, p. 40
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            together with an “interpretation” operation allowing us to regard its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terms"} terms
            as
            %em codes
            or
            %em names
            for actual types. Thus we have a rule such as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi 𝒰
                    %mrow
                      %mi El
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{A:\mathcal{U}}{El(A)\;type}
          %p
            saying that for each term
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            of the type universe
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            there is an actual type
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi El
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} El(A)
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Egbert+Rijke"} Egbert Rijke
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Homotopy+Type+Theory"} Introduction to Homotopy Type Theory
          %p
            Conversely, with notation as used at
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object+classifier+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} object classifier in an (infinity,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mo ′
                  %mi El
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = 'El(A)'
            to indicate that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is the
            %em name
            of the type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi El
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} El(A)
            in the type universe.
          %p We usually also have operations on the universe corresponding to (but not identical to) type formers, such as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi 𝒰
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi B
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi 𝒰
                    %mrow
                      %mi π
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi 𝒰
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{A:\mathcal{U}\quad B:A\to \mathcal{U}}{\pi(A, B) : \mathcal{U}}
          %p
            with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equality
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi El
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi Π
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi El
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi El
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} El(\pi(A,B))=\Pi \, El(A)\, El(B)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgmental+equality"} judgmental equality
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+homotopy+type+theory"} equivalence
            (i.e. we have a rule which gives us a canonical term of the equivalence type), we may speak of a
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weakly+Tarski+universe"} weakly Tarski universe
            (
            %a{:href => "#Gallozzi14"}> Gallozzi 14, p. 49-50
            ).
          %p
            We can give a slightly different definition of weakly Tarski universe using
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/typal+equality"} typal equality
            in either a larger universe or a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory+with+type+variables"} dependent type theory with type variables
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type#IdentityTypesBetweenTypes"} identity types between types
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                in a larger universe
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U'
                we can consider a universe
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒰
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
                and with the usual rules for the relative reflection
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi el
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi 𝒰
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} el(a):\mathcal{U}'
                for any
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo :
                        %mi 𝒰
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:\mathcal{U}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computation+rules"} computation rules
                for the reflections
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi El
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} El
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi El
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} El'
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒰
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
                inside
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒰
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}'
                based on typal equality, which gives us canonical elements of the identity types
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Id
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒰
                          %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi π
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi el
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi el
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi el
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi π
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id_{\mathcal{U}'}(\pi'(el(a),el(b)),el(\pi(a,b)))
                and similarly for the other type formers.
            %li
              %p
                in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory+with+type+variables"} dependent type theory with type variables
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type#IdentityTypesBetweenTypes"} identity types between types
                we can similarly consider a universe
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒰
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
                and with the usual rules for the relative reflection
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi el
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} el(a) \; \mathrm{type}
                for any
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo :
                        %mi 𝒰
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:\mathcal{U}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computation+rules"} computation rules
                for the reflections
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi El
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} El
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi El
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} El'
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒰
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}
                based on typal equality, which gives us canonical elements of the identity types between types
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi π
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi el
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi el
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi el
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi π
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Id}(\pi'(el(a),el(b)),el(\pi(a,b)))
                and similarly for the other type formers.
          %p If the containing universe or dependent type theory with type variables is univalent, the two definitions of a weak Tarski universe turn out to coincide.
          %p
            The three notions of Tarski universe can be ordered by generality: Every Tarski universe is weakly Tarski by equivalences, because both definitional equality of types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ≡
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \equiv B
            and the identity types between two types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = B
            imply that the two types of equivalent
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \simeq B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ≡
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \equiv B
            implies that two types are identified
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = B
          %p
            Since each type former is independent of each other, one could also have mixed versions of Tarski universes, where some of the type formers are strictly Tarski and some are weakly Tarski. This leads to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mn 2
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^n
            possible Tarski universes, where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            is the number of type formers in a type theory, and the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mn 2
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^n
            type theories are only
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partially+ordered"} partially ordered
            by generality. Internally in an ambient universe, that number becomes
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mn 3
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3^n
          %p
            Universes defined internally via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction-recursion"} induction-recursion
            are stricty Tarski. Weakly Tarski universes are easier to obtain in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semantics"} semantics
            (see
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#CategoricalSemantics"} below
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objective+type+theory"} objective type theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definitional+equality"} definitional equality
          %h3#other_universes Other universes
          %p
            There are other universes which one could use. For example, any model of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/material+set+theory"} material set theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structural+set+theory"} structural set theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            would suffice. Material set theories become Tarski universes by the type family
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi V
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi V
                  %mi y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:V \vdash \mathrm{El}(x) \coloneqq \sum_{y:V} y \in x
          %p and structural set theories become Tarski universes by the type family
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi V
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:V \vdash \mathrm{El}(x) \coloneqq \mathrm{hom}(1, x)
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1:\mathcal{E}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separator"} separator
          %p
            Thus, in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            with a separate
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgment"} judgment
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ZFC"} ZFC
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ETCS"} ETCS
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#UniverseEnlargement Universe enlargement
          %p
            Both
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coq"} Coq
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Agda"} Agda
            support
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universe+polymorphism"} universe polymorphism
            to deal with the issue of universe enlargement. Moreover, Coq supports
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/typical+ambiguity"} typical ambiguity
          %h3#extensionality_principle_of_type_universes Extensionality principle of type universes
          %p
            The extensionality principle of type universes is given by the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence+axiom"} univalence axiom
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tarski+universes"} Tarski universes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ,
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (U, T)
            states that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transport"} transport
            across the universal type family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is an equivalence of types for all small types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A:U
            and
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo :
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B:U
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Russell+universes"} Russell universes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            states that the recursively defined function
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} idToEquiv
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{idToEquiv}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A:U
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo :
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B:U
            to equivalences between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A:U
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo :
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B:U
          %h3#cumulativity Cumulativity
          %p
            A tower of universes is
            %strong cumulative
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒰
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A:\mathcal{U}_i
            implies
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒰
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A:\mathcal{U}_{i+1}
            (rather than, say,
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Lift
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒰
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Lift(A):\mathcal{U}_{i+1}
          %p
            Cumulative Russell universes have some issues; see for instance
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Luo12"} Luo 12
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coq"} Coq
                uses Russell style universes. For practical purposes, it also has cumulativity, although there is some question (perhaps mainly semantic) of whether this is true internally or whether it uses casts that are simply hidden from the user.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Agda"} Agda
                uses non-cumulative Russell style universes.
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#UFP13"} UFP13
                (first edition) uses cumulative Russell style universes.
          %h3#CategoricalSemantics Categorical semantics
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence"} Univalent
            %a{:href => "#RussellStyle"} Russell universes
            have been shown to be interpreted in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type-theoretic+model+categories"} type-theoretic model categories
            presenting the base
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            (
            %a{:href => "#KapulkinLumsdaineVoevodsky12"}> Kapulkin-Lumsdaine-Voevodsky 12
            )
          %p
            and more generally presenting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} (∞,1)-toposes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-presheaves
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elegant+Reedy+categories"} elegant Reedy categories
            (
            %a{:href => "#Shulman13"}> Shulman 13
            ).
          %p
            Discussion for general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} (∞,1)-toposes
            (of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-sheaves
            %a{:href => "#TarskiStyle"} weakly Tarski
            (
            %a{:href => "#Gallozzi14"}> Gallozzi 14, p. 49-50
            ) is in (
            %a{:href => "#GepnerKock12"}> Gepner-Kock 12
            ).
          %p
            For more on this see the respective sections at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation+between+type+theory+and+category+theory"} relation between type theory and category theory
          %h2#other_types_of_types Other types of types
          %p
            There is other notions of type of types. These are typically given by a universe-indexed dependent sum type, or in dependent type theory without type universes, by a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/record+type+with+type+fields"} record type with type fields
          %p
            Suppose we have a Russell universe
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            or a Tarski universe
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ,
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (U, T)
            and a function
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo :
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                      %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P:U \to \mathrm{Prop}_U
            = succeed "-small" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            is given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum+type"} dependent sum type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi U
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{A:U} P(A)
            for Russell universes and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi U
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{A:U} T(P(A))
            for Tarski universes.
          %p
            Since universes are internal models of type theory, in a dependent type theory with a separate
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgment"} judgment
            = succeed "-small" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo :
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A:U
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \; \mathrm{type}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo :
                  %mi U
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                    %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P:U \to \mathrm{Prop}_U
            which takes types to propositons is now an operator on types, which is defined using
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inference+rules"} inference rules
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} proptrunc
                        %mrow
                          %mi P
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isProp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma \vdash P(A) \; \mathrm{type}} \quad \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{proptrunc}_{P(A)}:\mathrm{isProp}(P(A)) \; \mathrm{type}}
          %p
            Examples of such
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            definable from the existing type formers in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            include
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isProp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{isProp}
              , which results in the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+all+propositions"} type of all propositions
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isFinite
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{isFinite}
              , which results in the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+all+finite+types"} type of all finite types
            %li
              given a type
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [(-) \simeq T]
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+types"} equivalent
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %li
              given a type
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [(-) \hookrightarrow T]
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+preorder"} subtype preorder
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+types"} embed into
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %p
            The resulting
            %strong
              type of types which satisfy
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            is denoted by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Type
                      %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Type}_P
          %p
            Care must be taken for which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            one could use to define the type of all types which satisfy
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+type"} unit type
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝟙
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{1}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≡
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝟙
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(A) \equiv A \to \mathbb{1}
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≡
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(A) \equiv \mathrm{isSet}(A)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Type
                    %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Type}_P
            always contains itself or its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+truncation"} set truncation
            in addition to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+type"} empty type
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Girard%27s+paradox"} Girard's paradox
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≡
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∨
                  %mo ¬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(A) \equiv \prod_{x:A} \prod_{y:A} (x =_A y) \vee \neg (x =_A y)
          %p
            the resulting
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Type
                    %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Type}_P
            contains its set truncation in addition to the empty type if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+excluded+middle"} principle of excluded middle
            holds for all propositions, resulting in
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Girard%27s+paradox"} Girard's paradox
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Type
                    %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Type}_P
            for
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≡
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∨
                  %mo ¬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(A) \equiv \prod_{x:A} \prod_{y:A} (x =_A y) \vee \neg (x =_A y)
          %p if one doesn’t have excluded middle in the type theory.
          %p
            Now, supposing that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            has the above rules for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(A)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Type
                    %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Type}_P
            could be presented either as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Russell+universe"} Russell universe
            or a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tarski+universe"} Tarski universe
            in a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            in the type theory is literally an element of the type of types which satisfy
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Type
                    %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Type}_P
            are only indices of a type family
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{El}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+type"} finite type
            in the type theory is only
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+small+type"}
              essentially
              = succeed "-small" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Type
                        %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Type}_P
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+Tarski+universes"} weak Tarski universes
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgmentally+equal"} judgmentally equal
            to an
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(A)
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Type
                    %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A:\mathrm{Type}_P
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+Tarski+universes"} strict Tarski universes
          %p
            For weak Tarski type of types with satisfy
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(A)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi B
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi e
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} congform
                        %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type} \quad \Gamma \vdash B \; \mathrm{type} \quad \Gamma \vdash e:A \simeq B}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{congform}_P(e):P(A) \simeq P(B) \; \mathrm{type}}
          %h4#as_a_strict_tarski_universe As a strict Tarski universe
          %p
            As a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+Tarski+universe"} strict Tarski universe
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            is given by the following
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+deduction"} natural deduction
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inference+rules"} inference rules
          %p
            Formation rules for the type of all types which satisfy
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
