                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+type+theory"} univalent type theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hierarchy+of+universes"} hierarchy of universes
          %h2#references References
          %p
            Type universes in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin-L%C3%B6f+type+theory"} Martin-Löf type theory
            originate in un-stratified and hence inconsistent form with
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Per+Martin-L%C3%B6f"}> Per Martin-Löf
              , §2.7.1 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Theory of Types
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelt/martin-lof/master/pdfs/martin-loef1971%20-%20A%20Theory%20of%20Types.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/MartinLoef1971-ATheoryOfTypes.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p and then in stratified and consistent form in
          %ul
            %li#MartinLof75
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Per+Martin-L%C3%B6f"}> Per Martin-Löf
              , §1.10 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em An intuitionistic theory of types: predicative part
              = succeed "," do
                %em Logic Colloquium ‘73, Proceedings of the Logic Colloquium
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 80
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0049-237X(08)71945-1"} doi:10.1016/S0049-237X(08)71945-1
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/summary?doi=10.1.1.131.926"} CiteSeer
          %p elaborated on in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Per+Martin-L%C3%B6f"} Per Martin-Löf
              (notes by
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giovanni+Sambin"} Giovanni Sambin
              = succeed "," do
                %em Universes
              = succeed "," do
                %em Intuitionistic type theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://archive-pml.github.io/martin-lof/pdfs/Bibliopolis-Book-retypeset-1984.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/MartinLofIntuitionisticTypeTheory.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            which also introduces (p. 48) the distinction into notions of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Russell+universes"} Russell universes
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tarski+universes"} Tarski universes
          %p Further discussion in
          %ul
            %li#Hofmann95
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Hofmann"}> Martin Hofmann
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Universes
              = succeed "," do
                %em Syntax and semantics of dependent types
              = succeed "," do
                %em Extensional concepts in intensional type theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.lfcs.inf.ed.ac.uk/reports/95/ECS-LFCS-95-327/"} ECS-LFCS-95-327
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/HofmannExtensionalIntensionalTypeTheory.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4471-0963-1"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4471-0963-1
          %p Review and further discussion:
          %ul
            %li#Palmgren
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Erik+Palmgren"}> Erik Palmgren
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On Universes in Type Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %em Twenty-Five Years of Constructive Type Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www2.math.uu.se/~palmgren/universe.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1093/oso/9780198501275.003.0012"} doi:10.1093/oso/9780198501275.003.0012
          %p
            Introduction with an eye towards
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
          %ul
            %li#UFP13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Univalent+Foundations+Project"}> Univalent Foundations Project
              , §1.3 in
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopy+Type+Theory+--+Univalent+Foundations+of+Mathematics"} Homotopy Type Theory – Univalent Foundations of Mathematics
              (2013) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://homotopytypetheory.org/book/"}> web
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://hottheory.files.wordpress.com/2013/03/hott-online-323-g28e4374.pdf"} pdf
          %p Definition of weakly Tarski universes:
          %ul
            %li#Hofmann
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Hofmann"}> Martin Hofmann
                , section 2.1.6 of
                %em Syntax and semantics of dependent types
                (
                %a{:href => "http://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/summary?doi=10.1.1.36.8985"}> web
                )
            %li#Luo12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zhaohui+Luo"}> Zhaohui Luo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Notes on Universes in Type Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.cs.rhul.ac.uk/home/zhaohui/universes.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Gallozzi14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cesare+Gallozzi"}> Cesare Gallozzi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Constructive Set Theory from a Weak Tarski Universe
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1411.5591"} arXiv:1411.5591
          %p
            Detailed discussion of the type of types in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coq"} Coq
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adam+Chlipala"}> Adam Chlipala
              ,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://adam.chlipala.net/cpdt/"} Certified programming with dependent types
              –
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://adam.chlipala.net/cpdt/html/Universes.html"} Library Universes
          %p See also around slide 8 of the survey
          %ul
            %li
              Frade,
              %em Calculus of inductive constructions
              (2008/2009) (
              %a{:href => "http://www3.di.uminho.pt/~mjf/pub/SFV-CIC-2up.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+proof"} formal proof
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            that the type of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+n-types"} homotopy n-types
            is not itself a homotopy
            = succeed "-type" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-type)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolai+Kraus"}> Nicolai Kraus
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Sattler"} Christian Sattler
              %em
                The universe
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒰
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}_n
                is not an
                = succeed "-type" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              May 2013 (
              %a{:href => "http://red.cs.nott.ac.uk/~ngk/universes.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-Categorical
            semantics for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence"} univalent
            type universes is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#KapulkinLumsdaineVoevodsky12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Kapulkin"}> Chris Kapulkin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+LeFanu+Lumsdaine"} Peter LeFanu Lumsdaine
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Voevodsky"} Vladimir Voevodsky
                %em The Simplicial Model of Univalent Foundations
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1211.2851"}> arXiv:1211.2851
                )
            %li#Shulman13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Shulman"}> Michael Shulman
                ,
                %em The univalence axiom for elegant Reedy presheaves
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1307.6248"}> arXiv:1307.6248
                )
            %li#GepnerKock12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Gepner"}> David Gepner
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joachim+Kock"} Joachim Kock
                %em Univalence in locally cartesian closed ∞-categories
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1208.1749"}> arXiv:1208.1749
                )
          %p
            Relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+types"} injective types
          %ul
            %li#Escardo19
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mart%C3%ADn+Escard%C3%B3"}> Martín Escardó
              ,
              %em Injectives types in univalent mathematics
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.01211"}> arXiv:1903.01211
              )
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li#Rathjen
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Rathjen"}> Michael Rathjen
                ,
                %em The strength of Martin-Löf type theory with superuniverse. Part I
                %a{:href => "https://www1.maths.leeds.ac.uk/~rathjen/Super.pdf"} pdf
            %li#SEP
              %p
                Stanford Encyclopedia of Philosophy,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://plato.stanford.edu/entries/type-theory/#6"} Type theory – Extensions of type systems, Polymorphism, Paradoxes
            %li#Luo11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zhaohui+Luo"}> Zhaohui Luo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Contextual analysis of word meanings in type-theoretical semantics
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Logical Aspects of Computational Linguistics
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.cs.rhul.ac.uk/home/zhaohui/LACL11.pdf"} pdf
        .revisedby
